\section{Source scale}{

Item difficulty is the mean of its absolute adjacent-category thresholds, and
source scale identification and slopes are retained without rescaling:
\itemize{
\item \strong{\code{mirt}:} Unidimensional \code{Rasch}, \verb{2PL}, \code{gpcm}, \code{gpcmIRT}, and \code{rsm}
items with positive slopes and ordinary \verb{0..(K-1)} category scores are
supported; graded-response, guessing, custom-scoring, and multidimensional
models are refused. For \code{gpcmIRT} and \code{rsm}, the category offset is
included as \code{b - c / a}. Person estimates are EAP with conditional
posterior SDs in \code{SE}.
\item \strong{\code{TAM}:} Unidimensional MML fits (\code{tam.mml}, \code{tam.mml.mfr}) with positive
constant adjacent-category slopes are supported; \code{tam.jml} and
multidimensional (\code{ndim > 1}) fits are refused. Multi-facet \code{tam.mml.mfr}
fits combine facet effects per design cell and retain the original
coefficient table in \code{source$native_parameters}. Transformed item SEs are
retained only when the location is a scalar multiple of a single fixed-slope
source coefficient; otherwise \code{SE} is \code{NA}. Person estimates retain source
EAP and conditional posterior SD, while \code{TAM::tam.personfit()} uses WLE
scores (recorded in \code{FitBasis}). TAM-native AIC, BIC, and \code{aBIC} are kept
under \verb{Native*} fields with \code{ICStatus = "imported_native_descriptive"} and
\code{ICEligible = FALSE}.
\item \strong{\code{eRm}:} Conditional ML cumulative easiness coefficients from \code{RM},
\code{PCM}, or \code{RSM} are negated and differenced into absolute adjacent-category
difficulties, with scalar-transformed item-location SEs and ML person
parameters (retaining \code{source_extrapolated} flags for extremes).
}
}

\section{Imported uncertainty}{

Imported SEs retain the source package's interpretation. The measurement-side
diagnostics do not reconstruct the joint parameter covariance, so joint facet
chi-square statistics, degrees of freedom and p-values are unavailable.
Posterior SDs do not supply sampling SEs for separation reliability.
Other separation summaries require valid SEs for every finite estimate and
remain descriptive. Imported Wright maps show points only: source uncertainty
conventions do not establish one common confidence-interval calculation.
Re-import older saved bundles from the existing source-package fit to update
difficulties, thresholds and uncertainty labels. The \code{mirt} and \code{TAM} paths
accept \code{compute_fit = TRUE} when source fit statistics are needed; no model
re-estimation is required.
}

\section{Scope}{

Use \code{summary()} for source-scale tables and \code{plot()} for a point-only Wright
map. Available source fit statistics remain in the facet and diagnostic
tables. Native model curves, comprehensive \code{\link[=mfrm_results]{mfrm_results()}} reports,
response-level diagnostics, \code{\link[=run_qc_pipeline]{run_qc_pipeline()}}, bias/DIF analysis, anchoring
and portable calibration are unavailable for imported bundles. This is a
one-way fitted-object import of the documented fields.
}

